  "answer_text": "The thin, lightweight Columbia PFG shirts go by a few popular names depending on the style. Here are the main ones:\n\n1. **PFG Bahama Shirt** \u2013 Featuring lightweight nylon fabric in a roomy Relaxed Fit, this fishing shirt dries fast, keeps you cool, and blocks sun. It's one of the most popular and recognizable thin PFG shirts.\n\n2. **Terminal Tackle Shirt** \u2013 Made from 100% recycled polyester for lightweight comfort on the water. It's a go-to thin long-sleeve tee style.\n\n3. **Tamiami Long Sleeve Shirt** \u2013 This long-sleeve fishing shirt features a casual fit and an easy snap-up design with cool moisture-wicking fabric and UPF 50 sun protection.\n\n4. **Tidal Tee** \u2013 The women's equivalent of the Terminal Tackle, also a thin, lightweight option.\n\n5. **Tidal Deflector / Terminal Deflector** \u2013 If you get hot and sweaty on the water, this is one of the best fishing shirts for cooling, made with Omni-Freeze\u2122 ZERO Ice technology using touch-activated cooling fabric.\n\nThe most iconic and commonly referenced \"thin PFG shirt\" is usually the **PFG Bahama** or the **Terminal Tackle** \u2014 both are known for their ultra-lightweight, breathable feel. The PFG line, which stands for **Performance Fishing Gear**, offers anglers advanced technology along with a cool, laid-back style.",
